{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you're stuck offline. On our side your work laptop shows as offline, so it can't reach the internet right now. Please try these steps in order and check after each one whether websites load:\n1. Check whether other devices on your home Wi-Fi (your phone, a TV) can load websites. If none of them can, the problem is your home network or internet provider, not the laptop.\n2. On the laptop, turn Wi-Fi off and back on. If that doesn't help, forget your home network and reconnect to it.\n3. Restart the laptop.\n4. Restart your home router: unplug it for about 30 seconds, plug it back in, and give it a few minutes to come back up.\n5. If it's still not working, connect the laptop to your phone's hotspot or plug in a network cable. That tells us whether the laptop itself is okay.\nOnce you're back online, please leave the laptop on and signed in for about 30 minutes. It hasn't checked in with our systems for about 12 days and needs to catch up on updates.\nPlease reply and tell me whether your other devices work and which step (if any) fixed it. If nothing works, even on the hotspot, let us know and we'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), account active, not blocked, vpn_access true, no failed logins. Laptop BL-LT-0107 shows online=false, last_checkin 2026-09-29, warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Offline status fits the reported no internet (KB-014). Sent the user the KB-014 home Wi-Fi steps (Wi-Fi toggle/forget network, restart, router restart, hotspot/wired test) and asked whether other devices on her network work. Also asked her to stay online and signed in for 30 min so the overdue management check-in can catch up (KB-018). Next: once she reports back, re-run check_device_status to confirm a fresh check-in. If the laptop still can't connect on a hotspot or wired connection, escalate to Tier 2 as a possible laptop network adapter/driver fault. If it comes back online but still doesn't check in after a restart, escalate per KB-018.",
